{"In RecoveryAuthnCodeInputLoginBean, credentialModelOpt.get() is called without checking isPresent(), causing NoSuchElementException if no recovery credential exists for the user": 0.8367887139320374, "RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialModel.createFromValues() never calls setId(), so federated credentials have null ID causing NPE or silent failure when removeStoredCredentialById is called": 0.3556317687034607, "BackwardsCompatibilityUserStorage.supportsCredentialType claims support for recovery-authn-codes but disableCredentialType does not handle that type, so disabling recovery codes for federated users will not actually remove/disable them": 0.8466705083847046, "Recovery code validation in BackwardsCompatibilityUserStorage.isValid() only checks if code exists via anyMatch() but never removes/consumes the used code, allowing same recovery code to be reused indefinitely": 0.8623955845832825, "When all recovery codes are exhausted for federated users, removeStoredCredentialById() only removes from local storage, not from the user storage provider": 0.778885543346405, "Recovery codes in BackwardsCompatibilityUserStorage.updateCredential() are stored as plaintext JSON array instead of being hashed with SHA-512 like the normal Keycloak flow": 0.6641032695770264, "Inconsistent storage format vs validation: getCredentials() calls createFromValues() which re-hashes codes, but isValid() reads raw credentialData and compares directly against user input without hashing": 0.7471860647201538}